f%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Falzheimers-and-dementia-misconceptions-and-surprising-facts-2018-10%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3EAlzheimer's%20disease%3C%2Fa%3E%20two-and-a-half%20years%20ago%2C%20it%20soon%20became%20apparent%20that%20she%20would%20need%2024-hour%20care.%20%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EI%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fwrote-book-working-full-time-productivity-habits-helped-sacrificing-sleep-2025-12%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Ework%20full-time%3C%2Fa%3E%20and%20live%20in%20a%20small%20apartment%20with%20two%20kids%2C%20so%20caring%20for%20her%20myself%20or%20having%20her%20move%20in%20with%20me%20was%20not%20an%20option.%20Thankfully%20(after%20nine%20months%20and%20tons%20of%20red%20tape)%2C%20I%20was%20able%20to%20get%20her%20into%20a%20Medicaid%20program%20and%20arrange%20full-time%20in-home%20care%20for%20her.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EWhat%20I%20didn't%20expect%20was%20that%20caring%20for%20her%20would%20still%20be%20a%20full-time%20job.%20Don't%20get%20me%20wrong.%20I%20love%20my%20mother%20and%20want%20to%20help%20her.%20Her%20condition%20is%20heartbreaking%2C%20and%20I'm%20extremely%20grateful%20that%20she%20has%20people%20with%20her%20to%20manage%20her%20moment-by-moment%20care%20needs%2C%20like%20cooking%2C%20cleaning%2C%20grooming%2C%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fbeing-organized-helped-me-through-my-cancer-diagnosis-and-treatment-2023-3%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Emedication%20reminders%3C%2Fa%3E%2C%20and%20making%20sure%20she%20stays%20safe.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EStill%2C%20I%20never%20expected%20how%20much%20work%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fcaregiving-grandparent-nursing-assistant-caring-for-family-member-2026-7%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Ecaregiving%20for%20an%20elderly%3C%2Fa%3E%20parent%20would%20be%2C%20even%20if%20I'm%20not%20providing%20direct%2024%2F7%20care.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%226a366df8-6d03-4abd-b05a-e65b3d253689%5C%22%3EMy%20mom%20is%20reliant%20on%20me%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3EMy%20mother%20is%20extremely%20reliant%20on%20me%20emotionally.%20She%20can%20still%20use%20her%20phone%2C%20so%20I%20get%20about%2020%20to%2030%20texts%20and%20about%20one%20to%2010%20phone%20calls%20from%20her%20daily.%20%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EEach%20time%20her%20aide%20gives%20her%20medication%2C%20she%20texts%20me%20to%20ask%20what%20it's%20called.%20She%20asks%20me%20multiple%20times%20a%20day%20when%20I%20will%20see%20her%20next%2C%20even%20after%20I%20answer%20her.%20It's%20endless%20repeated%20questions%2C%20confusion%2C%20and%20fears.%20I%20can't%20respond%20to%20everything%2C%20but%20I%20have%20to%20respond%20sometimes%2C%20and%20it's%20a%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fquick-morning-routines-improve-your-day-2017-6%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Econstant%20interruption%3C%2Fa%3E%20to%20my%20day.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EI%20live%20five%20minutes%20away%20from%20her%2C%20so%20anytime%20she%20needs%20something%2C%20it%20falls%20on%20my%20husband%20or%20me.%20She%20can%20no%20longer%20shop%20or%20run%20errands%20and%20often%20needs%20help%20with%20this%20or%20that%20around%20her%20house.%20We%20are%20there%20multiple%20times%20a%20week%20helping%20her.%20She%20tends%20to%20lose%20things%2C%20break%20things%2C%20or%20cause%20other%20problems%20at%20home%20that%20require%20outside%20support.%20I%20also%20make%20it%20a%20practice%20to%20spend%20one%20afternoon%20a%20week%20with%20her%20just%20spending%20time%20together.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%2286e6d63b-5fb6-4931-977d-d5be1528c2ae%5C%22%3EI'm%20always%20on%20the%20phone%2C%20figuring%20out%20paperwork%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3EThen%2C%20there's%20the%20health%20insurance%20paperwork%20and%20phone%20calls%2C%20doctor%20phone%20calls%2C%20calls%20with%20caregivers%2C%20calls%20with%20other%20family%20members%2C%20etc.%20Not%20a%20day%20goes%20by%20that%20I'm%20not%20on%20the%20phone%20with%20someone%20or%20an%20organization%20that%20helps%20provide%20her%20care.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EI%20also%20take%20my%20mother%20to%20every%20doctor's%20appointment%20she%20has%2C%20which%20can%20be%20quite%20frequent.%20I%20manage%20her%20medication%2C%20which%20includes%20renewals%2C%20pharmacy%20pick-ups%2C%20and%20filling%20her%20medication%20trays%20weekly%20for%20her%20aides.%20I%20also%20manage%20her%20finances%20and%20pay%20all%20bills.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EOn%20top%20of%20all%20this%2C%20there's%20almost%20always%20some%20emergency%20each%20week.%20Last%20week%2C%20my%20mother%20locked%20two%20different%20doors%20in%20her%20apartment%20from%20the%20inside%2C%20making%20the%20rooms%20inaccessible%2C%20and%20we%20had%20to%20call%20an%20emergency%20handyman%20to%20get%20them%20opened.%20We%20then%20had%20to%20go%20out%20and%20buy%20new%20doorknobs%20and%20figure%20out%20how%20to%20temporarily%20disable%20the%20remaining%20doorknobs%20in%20her%20house%20so%20she%20wouldn't%20lock%20them%2C%20too.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EI'm%20on%20the%20phone%20with%20her%20aides%2C%20my%20other%20family%20members%2C%20and%20her%20doctors%20to%20discuss%20how%20to%20handle%20things.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%22e52608ec-cab4-417e-9f40-aa4049521ebf%5C%22%3EI%20grieve%20for%20who%20my%20mom%20once%20was%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3EThe%20whole%20thing%20is%20just%20so%20much%20to%20manage%2C%20and%20so%20stressful%2C%20too.%20I%20spend%20many%20sleepless%20nights%20wondering%20how%20I'm%20going%20to%20do%20all%20the%20things%20I%20need%20to%20do%20for%20her%2C%20and%20how%20I%20can%20possibly%20do%20it%20all%20for%20the%20next%20few%20years%2C%20as%20she%20continues%20to%20live%20with%20her%20condition.%20She%20is%20in%20her%20late%2070s%2C%20so%20it%20may%20still%20be%20another%20few%20years%20before%20she%20lives%20with%20this%20condition.%20Alzheimer's%20is%20progressive%20and%20incurable%2C%20and%20while%20the%20caregiving%20tasks%20will%20evolve%2C%20they%20will%20continue%20to%20be%20here%20for%20the%20rest%20of%20her%20life.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EWhile%20I%20grieve%20for%20my%20mother%20and%20what%20her%20life%20has%20become%2C%20sometimes%20I%20feel%20like%20I%20have%20little%20time%20to%20feel%20sadness.%20The%20kind%20of%20care%20I%20provide%20for%20her%20is%20so%20relentless%20and%20so%20stressful%20that%20there%20is%20almost%20no%20time%20for%20me%20to%20even%20consider%20my%20own%20feelings%20about%20what's%20happening%20to%20her.%20When%20do%20I%20get%20to%20say%20goodbye%20if%20I'm%20knee-deep%20in%20the%20daily%20tasks%20that%20are%20necessary%20to%20keep%20her%20safe%2C%20all%20while%20she%20deteriorates%20before%20my%20eyes%3F%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EI%20know%20that%20one%20day%20I'll%20look%20back%20at%20this%20time%20and%20remember%20all%20the%20little%20moments%20we%20had%20together%20%E2%80%94%20the%20way%20I%20held%20her%20hand%20as%20we%20took%20a%20walk%20through%20her%20neighborhood%2C%20the%20contented%20sighs%20from%20her%20on%20the%20other%20end%20of%20the%20phone%20while%20I%20reassured%20her%20again%20that%20I%20would%20see%20her%20soon.%20I%20know%20she%20would%20appreciate%20all%20the%20tasks%20I%20do%20for%20her%20if%20she%20understood%20what%20was%20going%20on%20around%20her.%20I%20know%20that%20each%20thing%20I%20do%20is%20an%20act%20of%20love.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EBut%20I%20am%20drowning%20in%20these%20caregiving%20tasks%2C%20and%20sometimes%20wonder%20how%20I'm%20going%20to%20make%20it%20through%20the%20next%20bunch%20of%20years%20with%20my%20mental%20health%20intact.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cdiv%3ERead%20the%20original%20article%20on%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fmy-mom-has-alzheimers-caregiving-never-really-stops-2026-8%5C%22%3EBusiness%20Insider%3C%2Fa%3E%3C%2Fdiv%3E%22%2C%22published%22%3A1785677881000%2C%22visual%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fi.insider.com%2F6a68b26fce52cb26b8394a56%3Fformat%3Djpeg%22%2C%22originID%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fmy-mom-has-alzheimers-caregiving-never-really-stops-2026-8%22%2C%22summary%22%3A%22I%20thought%20arranging%2024-hour%20care%20for%20my%20mom%20with%20Alzheimer's%20would%20ease%20the%20burden.%20Instead%2C%20I%20discovered%20how%20much%20caregiving%20remained.%22%2C%22author%22%3A%22insider%40insider.com%20(Wendy%20Wisner)%22%2C%22engagement%22%3A9%2C%22canonicalUrl%22%3A%22%22%2C%22cdnAmpUrl%22%3A%22%22%2C%22ampUrl%22%3A%22%22%7D%2C%7B%22title%22%3A%22After%20starting%20the%20tokenmaxxing%20panic%2C%20Uber's%20CTO%20is%20back%20with%20a%20very%20different%20AI%20story%22%2C%22content%22%3A%22%3Cfigure%3E%3Cimg%20width%3D%5C%221000%5C%22%20alt%3D%5C%22Uber%20CTO%20Praveen%20Neppalli%20Naga%5C%22%20src%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fi.insider.com%2F6a6cf95487737bff3ebda295%3Fformat%3Djpeg%5C%22%20height%3D%5C%22750%5C%22%3E%3Cfigcaption%3EUber%20CTO%20Praveen%20Neppalli%20Naga%3Cp%3EUber%3C%2Fp%3E%3C%2Ffigcaption%3E%3C%2Ffigure%3E%3Cul%3E%3Cli%3EA%20version%20of%20this%20story%20originally%20appeared%20in%20the%20BI%20Tech%20Memo%20newsletter.%3C%2Fli%3E%3Cli%3ESign%20up%20for%20the%20weekly%20%3Ca%20data-autoaffiliated%3D%5C%22false%5C%22%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fsubscription%2Fnewsletter%2Ftech-memo%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3EBI%20Tech%20Memo%20newsletter%20here%3C%2Fa%3E.%3C%2Fli%3E%3C%2Ful%3E%3Cp%3ERemember%20the%20executive%20who%20sparked%20the%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Ftokenmaxxing-debate-uber-exec-viral-ai-costs-2026-5%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Etokenmaxxing%20panic%3C%2Fa%3E%20earlier%20this%20year%20after%20saying%20Uber%20had%20already%20blown%20through%20its%202026%20budget%20for%20Anthropic's%20Claude%20Code%3F%20He's%20back%20with%20a%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fx.com%2FpraveenTweets%2Fstatus%2F2074605343439810922%3Fs%3D20%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Emore%20interesting%20lesson%3C%2Fa%3E%20about%20AI.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EUber%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fuber-coo-andrew-macdonald-ai-token-spending-harder-justify-2026-5%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3ECTO%20Praveen%20Neppalli%20Naga%3C%2Fa%3E%20says%20the%20company%20has%20started%20sending%20its%20best%20AI%20engineers%20into%20departments%20like%20finance%2C%20legal%2C%20marketing%2C%20customer%20support%2C%20HR%2C%20and%20procurement%20to%20study%20how%20people%20actually%20work%20before%20building%20AI%20tools%20with%20them.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EHe%20called%20these%20two-week%20teams%20%26quot%3BAgentic%20Pods.%26quot%3B%20Engineers%20spend%20the%20first%20few%20days%20shadowing%20employees%2C%20learning%20every%20step%20of%20a%20workflow%2C%20then%20quickly%20build%20and%20test%20software%20to%20improve%20it.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EThe%20results%20are%20striking.%20One%20financial%20planning%20process%20dropped%20from%2015%20hours%20to%2030%20minutes.%20Financial%20reports%20fell%20from%20two%20days%20to%2010%20minutes.%20Marketing%20quality%20checks%20shrank%20from%20two%20weeks%20to%20less%20than%20an%20hour.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3ENaga%20said%20the%20biggest%20gains%20rarely%20come%20from%20speeding%20up%20one%20task.%20They%20come%20from%20redesigning%20an%20entire%20workflow%20around%20AI%2C%20eliminating%20unnecessary%20approvals%2C%20replacing%20old%20software%2C%20and%20helping%20people%20make%20decisions%20faster.%20You%20can%20see%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fts-imagine-ai-roi-efficiency-2025-11%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Ethis%20at%20work%20here%3C%2Fa%3E%2C%20too.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3ESeveral%20tech%20executives%20compared%20the%20approach%20to%20Silicon%20Valley's%20fast-growing%20%26quot%3Bforward-deployed%20engineer%26quot%3B%20role.%20The%20twist%3F%20Instead%20of%20sending%20these%20AI%20experts%20to%20customers%2C%20Uber%20is%20deploying%20them%20inside%20its%20own%20business%20to%20find%20the%20next%20wave%20of%20productivity%20gains.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EPeter%20Wilczynski%2C%20chief%20product%20officer%20at%20Vantortech%2C%20jokingly%20dubbed%20the%20role%20the%20%26quot%3B%3Ca